{"name":"Key to the City","hex":"#bb9b7c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"key to the city","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An ornamental key sometimes given as a symbol of a freedom of the city."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/key_to_the_city"}],"entries":[{"title":"Key to the City (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Key to the City is a 1950 American romantic comedy film starring Clark Gable and Loretta Young as mayors who meet in San Francisco and fall in love."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/05/Key_to_the_City_FilmPoster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Key_to_the_City_(film)","wikidata":"Q2360724"},{"title":"Freedom of the City","blocks":[{"text":"The Freedom of the City is connected to the medieval concept of \"free status\", when city and town charters drew a distinction between freemen and vassals of a feudal lord. As such, freemen actually pre-date modern boroughs. Early freedom of the boroughs ceremonies had great importance in affirming that the recipient enjoyed privileges such as the right to trade and own property, and protection within the town."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Gold_%27Freedom_of_the_City_Box%27_for_Daniel_T._Patterson%2C_made_by_Jonathan_Wilmarth%2C_John_L._Moffat%2C_and_Joseph_Curtis%2C_New_York_City%2C_1832%2C_gold_-_Winterthur_Museum_-_DSC01333.JPG/330px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freedom_of_the_City","wikidata":"Q99864"},{"title":"City","blocks":[{"text":"A city is a human settlement of a substantial size. The term \"city\" has different meanings around the world and in some places the settlement can be very small. Even where the term is limited to larger settlements, there is no universally agreed definition of the lower numerical boundary for their size. In a more specific sense, a city can be defined as a permanent and densely populated place with administratively defined boundaries whose members work primarily on non-agricultural tasks. Cities generally have extensive systems for housing, transportation, sanitation, utilities, land use, production of goods, and communication. Their density facilitates interaction between people, government organizations, and businesses, sometimes benefiting different parties in the process, such as improving the efficiency of goods and service distribution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg/330px-Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City","wikidata":"Q515"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Hadfield_Freedom_of_the_City_of_Sheffield.jpg/500px-Hadfield_Freedom_of_the_City_of_Sheffield.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Hadfield_Freedom_of_the_City_of_Sheffield.jpg/1280px-Hadfield_Freedom_of_the_City_of_Sheffield.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Hadfield_Freedom_of_the_City_of_Sheffield.jpg/500px-Hadfield_Freedom_of_the_City_of_Sheffield.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Award to Sir Robert Hadfield by the City of Sheffield, 1939 (Hadfield Room, University of Sheffield)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHadfield_Freedom_of_the_City_of_Sheffield.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Antoon_van_den_Heuvel_-_Ferdinand_Receives_the_Keys_of_the_City_from_the_Virgin_of_Ghent.jpg/500px-Antoon_van_den_Heuvel_-_Ferdinand_Receives_the_Keys_of_the_City_from_the_Virgin_of_Ghent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Antoon_van_den_Heuvel_-_Ferdinand_Receives_the_Keys_of_the_City_from_the_Virgin_of_Ghent.jpg/1280px-Antoon_van_den_Heuvel_-_Ferdinand_Receives_the_Keys_of_the_City_from_the_Virgin_of_Ghent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Antoon_van_den_Heuvel_-_Ferdinand_Receives_the_Keys_of_the_City_from_the_Virgin_of_Ghent.jpg/500px-Antoon_van_den_Heuvel_-_Ferdinand_Receives_the_Keys_of_the_City_from_the_Virgin_of_Ghent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Ferdinand Receives the Keys of the City from the Virgin of Ghent\", print after a painting made by Antoon van den Heuvel for the Joyous Entry by the Cardinal-Infante Ferdinand into Ghent in 1635","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAntoon_van_den_Heuvel_-_Ferdinand_Receives_the_Keys_of_the_City_from_the_Virgin_of_Ghent.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/A_recipient_of_Freedom_of_the_City_of_London.jpg/500px-A_recipient_of_Freedom_of_the_City_of_London.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/A_recipient_of_Freedom_of_the_City_of_London.jpg/1280px-A_recipient_of_Freedom_of_the_City_of_London.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/A_recipient_of_Freedom_of_the_City_of_London.jpg/500px-A_recipient_of_Freedom_of_the_City_of_London.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A recipient of Freedom of the City of London, Nigel Cumberland, after his ceremony","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_recipient_of_Freedom_of_the_City_of_L